<title>NEW ZEALAND: Air NZ sees over NZ$100 mln in savings.</title>
<headline>Air NZ sees over NZ$100 mln in savings.</headline>
<dateline>AUCKLAND 1996-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Air New Zealand Ltd Managing Director Jim McCrea said on Wednesday the company's &quot;project save&quot; campaign would involve a significant number of layoffs but would result in over NZ$100 million in savings.</p>
<p>&quot;I'm not prepared to say how many people are involved but it's not insignificant,&quot; McCrea told the New Zealand Investment Conference.</p>
<p>&quot;But I will say that that project is worth over NZ$100 million.</p>
<p>&quot;That's hugely important in terms of offsetting the strong New Zealand dollar and a few other factors,&quot; McCrea said.  </p>
<p>Air New Zealand announced its cost-cutting plan in September last year, saying its aim was to align fixed costs to the more competitive conditions prevailing.</p>
<p>--Wellington Newsroom (64 4) 4734746</p>
